posts.body:
@KaBlooZio
I am completely willing to extend on the core features, in time. The first step is to modify and extend the default javascripts so that a solid foundation exists which emulates the default features that appear in Pokemon Fire Red / Leaf Green as closely as possible. After the core programming is finished, I intend to create several plugins which would be entirely optional to developers which would perform the tasks you're asking about.
Also, thanks for participating in the poll!

@Lihinel
Thank you for your kind words. I have no concerns regarding the reconstruction of the default battle system; I am confident in my ability to get it done the correct way in a reasonable amount of time.
Truth be told, I am eager to jump into it but professionalism dictates that I do not deviate from my initial work flow plans; I have a small number of tasks to complete before I get into the battle system.

@dbchest
Before you get too deep into the whole Patreon discussion, I just want to point out that because this is not crowdfunding for a particular game project, you will not be able to post links of any form for it here. You can do so on your own webpage, and link your webpage, but that's all.
That aside, I think this is a fantastic project that I think a lot of people are going to want to use... hopefully for more than Pokemon fangames, too!

@Nutty171
i intend to create a demo game for the finished project to flaunt its prowess, haha, but it will be just that; a demo game for the plugin package and nothing more.
@taarna23
thank you for your kinds words, and thank you for that information! honestly, i may have made that mistake, had you not said something. i am building a web page currently, so that is the path i will take for that; i have every intention of remaining in good standing with forum policies and general practices.
on a side note:
i would be thrilled to see developers use Beast Masters to create original content!

@PixelMister
you and me both! i have been a fan of two-dimensional, top-down pokemon games for as long as i can remember. my brother and i use to start new games and race to the finish when new versions would hit stores. rpgmaker is an amazing tool for creating video games, but i want to extend its potential so that i can create my own pokemon-esque project of good quality.
p.s. i have received your pm and i will get back to you soon.

@PixelMister
what is the maximum dimensions (in pixels) you can work with? also, i am sooo excited to dig into the battle system; i hope to begin development of that within a week or so.
i have included an updated screenshot of the plugin list for the project; yesterday i wrote the plugin which is going to allow multiple instances of the same actor to be allowed in the party at any given time, i.e. capture as many of the same beast as you want, which forced me to modify several of the plugins already in place. the new highlighted "Beasts" plugin is the plugin that supports multiple instances of the same beast.

@PixelMister
i have not decided which art style i will pursue for Beast Masters yet, but i am leaning towards hand-drawn portraits.
the image below is a visual representation of the new "Beasts" plugin, working in tandem with the "BeastStatus" plugin. The "Beasts" plugin extends Game_Party to support the integration of multiple actor instances; i.e. players can capture as many of the same beast as they would like!

Definitely keeping my on this project! I've used the similar Pokemon Essentials in XP for years now, and I'd love to see all the new possibilities available with the newer engine.
As a side note, if you ever need an additional reference to game mechanics, I'd recommend Bulbapedia. It's pretty comprehensive. That, and I'm sure there's plenty of huge Pokemon fans around here (including myself
) that would be happy to help!

@VanillaBrocker
nice! i completely missed that material; i did not know that kind of material was public.
i think it is worth reiterating that i am not trying to duplicate the Pokemon series; i am emulating desirable features from Pokemon Fire Red and Leaf Green. Pokemon Essentials XP sounds like it was the perfect tool for creating non-commercial fan games of the Pokemon series, but my intentions for Beast Masters are different in that i want to give developers the opportunity to emulate some of the features existing in past Pokemon titles, while maintaining the developer's integrity of releasing original content to be sold commercially, if so desired.

